    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51515" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰχν-ευτής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tracker, hunter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.10
			</span></i>; of dogs which hunt by scent, ib.<i><span class="en">
				17
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπριδος ἰχνευτὰς
				ἀργυρέους σκύλακας</span>, of money given to a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταίρα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.15
			</span></i> (Marc. Arg.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰχνευταί, οἱ</span>, title of a satyric play by
			Sophocles (cf. v.
			<i><span class="en">
				298
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>detective</i> who <i>traces</i> missing persons, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRyl.</u>
				188.22
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχνεύμων</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.67
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				195
			</span></i>.</div>
